}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Araucaria}}|area_km2=647.19|population_census=508,460|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[Baliscano]], [[Andalusian language|Andalusian]]|cctld=.cbt|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|mapsize=280px|ethnic_groups_year=2023|ethnic_groups=68.4% [[Baliscans]]<br/> 31.6% [[Demographics of Balisca|others]]|population_census_rank=40th|GDP_PPP=$17.710 billion|GDP_PPP_per_capita=$34,831|GDP_PPP_year=2025|GDP_PPP_rank=42nd|GDP_PPP_rank_link=List of Baliscan regions by GDP|GDP_PPP_per_capita_rank=37th|GDP_PPP_per_capita_rank_link=List of Baliscan regions by GDP}}'''Cabu Traïdor''' ({{Langx|mxi|كَابُو تْرَايِيدُور|Kabu Traíður|treacherous cape}}; {{Langx|tpn|Y'Mbo-kará|4=waters of thieves}}) is a rugged and mountainous {{W|peninsula}}r [[Regions of Balisca|region]] in western [[Araucaria]], within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Its sole land border is with [[Juyú]] to the west, and is bounded on the other three sides by the [[Aethiopian Ocean]]. It has an area of {{convert|647.19|km2|abbr=on}} making it the smallest region of Balisca.  

The administrative seat and most-populous city in Cabo Traïdor is [[Daramazán]]. The region is situated in a oceanic setting with vast greenery and lush vegetation. The region has a {{W|humid subtropical climate}}, characterized by hot, humid summers and mild to cool winters. 

